#STEP1 HRT Atlas – Human HK Gene Mapping (GENCODE v19 → Ensembl 115)

Date: 21–23 October 2026  
Repository: HK-HR-Ref.Proteomes

## Data sources

- HRT Atlas v1.0 (Hounkpe et al., 2021): Original human housekeeping transcript list containing 2,833 unique ENST identifiers.
- GENCODE release 19 (GRCh37.p13): Historical transcript-to-gene reference annotation.
- Ensembl release 115 (GRCh38.p14), BioMart: Human protein-coding gene universe containing 23,262 genes before chromosome filtering.

GENCODE v19 was selected as the historical reference because HRT Atlas used GTEx v7 expression data, and GTEx v7 was annotated using GENCODE v19. This supports the selection of the historical reference without assuming that HRT Atlas explicitly documented GENCODE v19 as the origin of every published transcript identifier.

## Historical transcript-to-gene mapping

Mapped all 2,833 HRT ENST identifiers against the GENCODE v19 GTF annotation.

    Mapped ENST: 2,833 / 2,833 (100%)
    Unmapped ENST: 0
    Ambiguous ENST: 0
    Unique historical ENSG: 2,176

## Mapping to Ensembl 115

Compared the 2,176 historical GENCODE v19 ENSG identifiers with the complete Ensembl 115 protein-coding BioMart export, without chromosome filtering.

    Direct ENSG matches: 2,174
    Unmapped historical ENSG: 2
    Multiple BioMart annotations: 0

Identified two historical identifier changes:

    RBM8A: ENSG00000131795 → ENSG00000265241
    ACBD6: ENSG00000135847 → ENSG00000230124

Both target identifiers were confirmed to occur in the Ensembl 115 BioMart export.

    Final mapped ENSG: 2,176 / 2,176
    Unique E115 ENSG: 2,176
    Unresolved genes: 0
    Identifier collisions: 0

## Comparison with previous HRT mapping

Compared the new mapping against the previous HRT classification containing 2,172 HK genes.

    Shared HK genes: 2,168
    New-only HK genes: 8
    Old-only HK genes: 4

Five new-only genes originated from HRT transcripts that were not found in the original direct BioMart transcript mapping:

    GSS, SETD1B, BTBD6, FBXO21, PCSK7

Three new-only genes resulted from differences between historical and current transcript-to-gene assignments:

    TAF9, AL135905.2, C11orf98

A fourth transcript-to-gene assignment difference involved CHTF8, but its historically assigned ENSG was already represented in the previous HK set.

The four old-only ENSG identifiers were associated with these four transcript assignment differences and were not retained in the new reference-based classification.

## Final chromosome-restricted classification

Restricted the Ensembl 115 protein-coding BioMart background to chromosomes 1–22, X and Y. Calculated genomic gene length as end − start + 1 using Ensembl 115 BioMart coordinates.

    Original BioMart genes: 23,262
    Primary-chromosome genes: 20,084
    HRT reference-positive HK genes: 2,176
    HRT reference-negative genes: 17,908
    HRT HK genes excluded by chromosome filtering: 0
    Duplicate ENSG identifiers: 0

Final output:

    data/processed/human_all_genes_with_hrt_atlas_hk_status_gencode19.tsv

The term non-HK denotes absence from the HRT Atlas reference set, not independently verified non-housekeeping status. Mapping completeness does not establish biological completeness of the HK reference.

Original source files and previous mapping outputs were preserved.



# STEP2 Eisenberg & Levanon – Human HK Gene Mapping (RefSeq/HGNC → Ensembl 115)

Date: October 2026  
Repository: HK-HR-Ref.Proteomes

## Data sources

- Eisenberg & Levanon (2013): Original human housekeeping gene list containing 3,804 entries with HGNC gene symbols and RefSeq mRNA accession identifiers.
- Ensembl release 115 (GRCh38.p14), BioMart: Complete human protein-coding gene universe containing 23,262 genes before chromosome filtering.
- Ensembl 115 BioMart RefSeq mapping: 331,801 transcript rows, including Ensembl gene identifiers, transcript identifiers, transcript types, RefSeq mRNA identifiers and CCDS identifiers.
- Ensembl 115 BioMart HGNC mapping: Complete protein-coding gene export containing 23,262 ENSG entries, of which 22,390 have HGNC symbols.

The original Eisenberg list was mapped using RefSeq mRNA identifiers and HGNC symbols as independent mapping sources. The complete protein-coding BioMart exports were used instead of the previously Eisenberg-prefiltered HGNC export.

