# STEP3 Eisenberg vs HRT Atlas – Human HK Reference Comparison

Date: October 2026  
Repository: HK-HR-Ref.Proteomes

## Input datasets

Compared the final gene-level HK classifications generated from:

- Eisenberg & Levanon (2013), using the validated RefSeq/HGNC mapping.
- HRT Atlas v1.0 (Hounkpe et al., 2021), using the validated GENCODE v19 → Ensembl 115 mapping.

Both datasets were based on the same Ensembl 115 protein-coding gene universe restricted to chromosomes 1–22, X and Y.

The ENSG sets and genomic annotation columns were checked for consistency before classification.

    Shared gene universe: 20,084
    Unique ENSG in both datasets: 20,084
    Genomic annotations identical: YES

## HK reference comparison

    Eisenberg HK genes: 3,785
    HRT Atlas HK genes: 2,176

    HK in both references: 1,520
    HK only in Eisenberg: 2,265
    HK only in HRT: 655
    Eisenberg Unresolved: 5
    Reference-negative in both: 15,639

Detailed cross-classification:

    Eisenberg HK / HRT HK: 1,520
    Eisenberg HK / HRT non-HK: 2,265
    Eisenberg non-HK / HRT HK: 655
    Eisenberg non-HK / HRT non-HK: 15,639
    Eisenberg Unresolved / HRT HK: 1
    Eisenberg Unresolved / HRT non-HK: 4

The five Eisenberg-Unresolved genes were handled as a separate category and were not automatically included in either reference-negative or reference-exclusive groups.

## Overlap metrics

    Shared HK genes: 1,520
    Eisenberg HK shared with HRT: 40.16%
    HRT HK shared with Eisenberg: 69.85%

    HK union: 4,441
    Jaccard index: 0.3423

The 4,441-gene union includes one HRT-HK gene with unresolved Eisenberg status.

The two references show substantial disagreement despite representing the same biological concept. In particular, 2,265 genes classified as HK by Eisenberg are reference-negative in HRT, while 655 HRT-HK genes are reference-negative in Eisenberg.

The HRT Atlas HK set is therefore not simply a smaller subset of the Eisenberg HK set.

## Outputs

    data/processed/hk_reference_comparison/human_eisenberg_hrt_hk_comparison.tsv
    data/processed/hk_reference_comparison/hk_shared_eisenberg_hrt.tsv
    data/processed/hk_reference_comparison/hk_eisenberg_only.tsv
    data/processed/hk_reference_comparison/hk_hrt_only.tsv
    data/processed/hk_reference_comparison/eisenberg_unresolved_hrt_status.tsv
    data/processed/hk_reference_comparison/hk_reference_comparison_summary.tsv

Script:

    Compare_Eisenberg_vs_HRT_HK.py

The reference comparison demonstrates that HK classification depends substantially on the underlying reference definition and methodology.

Genes absent from either reference must not automatically be interpreted as biologically confirmed non-HK genes.

